    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d584">

                <pb facs="0901" n="773" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg773"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 584.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr.
                            Valera</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-06-13"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 13,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: * * * I take this occasion to communicate,
                    in connection with the note addressed to you on the 28th ultimo, the following
                    terms of a telegram from the Treasury Department on the 29th ultimo, to the
                    collector of customs, New Orleans, viz: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>You will give United States attorney and officers acting under his
                            direction, all aid that may he legally given to prevent the shipment of
                            arms by bark Adelina or other vessel in expedition against Cuba in
                            violation of neutrality laws.</p></quote></p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>T. F. BAYARD.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
